WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:20.033
was still fast asleep when the music started playing.

2
00:00:20.054 --> 00:00:26.297
"Not today, Alpha," she said with a groan.

3
00:00:26.837 --> 00:00:29.859
But as Ally pulled up the blankets, sadness washed over her.

4
00:00:30.479 --> 00:00:33.929
She wasn't in the pod—she was in the sewing room at Mateo's house.

5
00:00:36.731 --> 00:00:37.952
She blinked open her eyes.

6
00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:42.335
"Where's that music coming from?"

7
00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:44.296
"From out here!"

8
00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:46.398
Mateo called through the closed door.

9
00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:49.380
"Isn't this how Alpha wakes you up every day?"

10
00:00:50.661 --> 00:00:54.483
Ally didn't want to make Mateo feel bad, so she tried to wipe away her sadness.

11
00:00:54.503 --> 00:00:56.424
"Come on in."

12
00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:04.742
have to work," Mateo said, "but I have the whole day to look for the pod.

13
00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:07.683
I'll go to the museum as soon as it opens.

14
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:09.944
But first check this out."

15
00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:14.807
He read from an article on his phone: 'New City-Wide Parking Ordinance.

16
00:01:15.287 --> 00:01:20.110
The city of Sandville has begun implementing its new zero-tolerance policy.

17
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:24.392
All illegally parked vehicles will be towed to the impound lot.'

18
00:01:24.412 --> 00:01:28.254
"Maybe your pod got towed," Mateo said excitedly.

19
00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:31.116
"Let's go to the impound lot before your shift begins."

20
00:01:32.204 --> 00:01:33.565
"I'll be ready in a flash!"

21
00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:34.725
Ally cried.

22
00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:44.830
At the impound lot, there was a long line of humans waiting to claim their cars.

23
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.192
"This will take all day!"

24
00:01:50.073 --> 00:01:50.613
Ally moaned.

25
00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:52.114
"Maybe not."

26
00:01:52.614 --> 00:01:56.096
Mateo pointed to an area marked Oversize and Special Use Vehicles.

27
00:02:02.392 --> 00:02:06.394
They walked past parked campers, school buses, and a house on wheels.

28
00:02:09.336 --> 00:02:10.817
But Ally's pod wasn't there.

29
00:02:10.837 --> 00:02:15.119
"I really thought we would find it here," Mateo said.

30
00:02:15.139 --> 00:02:18.881
"I'll go to the museum now and meet you at the diner later."

31
00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:23.524
"Thanks, Mateo," Ally said as they headed in different directions.

32
00:02:23.544 --> 00:02:27.546
"Think positive," she told herself.

33
00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:29.627
"Hello there!"

34
00:02:30.127 --> 00:02:30.728
someone called.

35
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:31.880
Ally looked up.

36
00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:33.761
It was the artist, Sarah.

37
00:02:33.781 --> 00:02:37.263
"Thanks for the suggestion about the park.

38
00:02:38.043 --> 00:02:43.385
I found some amazing objects there—and a perfect location for my new sculpture!"

39
00:02:44.186 --> 00:02:44.946
Ally smiled.

40
00:02:44.966 --> 00:02:46.827
"I'm glad I was helpful."

41
00:02:46.847 --> 00:02:51.129
"I'd love to show you the site," Sarah said.

42
00:02:51.149 --> 00:02:52.549
"Are you free now?"

43
00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:57.932
"I have to go to work," Ally said, "but I'll stop by later."

44
00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.107
When Ally arrived at the diner, Barry was pacing around.

45
00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.131
thought you'd never get here!"

46
00:03:13.611 --> 00:03:13.971
he said.

47
00:03:13.991 --> 00:03:18.615
"I really want to learn how to levitate plates before the League of Rocket Scientists gala."

48
00:03:19.816 --> 00:03:22.498
Ally took a deep breath and reminded herself to be patient.

49
00:03:26.382 --> 00:03:29.064
"That's not realistic, Barry," she said.

50
00:03:29.084 --> 00:03:32.066
"It takes a long time to learn a trick like that."

51
00:03:33.107 --> 00:03:33.808
Barry frowned.

52
00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:36.410
"Well, I'm a super-fast learner."

53
00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.233
"Okay." Ally shrugged.

54
00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.755
"Let's get started.

55
00:03:43.136 --> 00:03:47.920
The first step is learning to make it look like you're stumbling without falling."

56
00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.502
"I've been practicing that skill.

57
00:03:50.742 --> 00:03:51.242
Watch this!"

58
00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:54.265
Barry demonstrated a perfect fake stumble.

59
00:03:59.429 --> 00:03:59.950
Ally thought.

60
00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.032
"He has been practicing!

61
00:04:02.844 --> 00:04:05.065
I guess it's time for the next part of my plan.

62
00:04:05.526 --> 00:04:06.546
I hope it works."

63
00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:12.610
Ally reached under the counter and pulled out the bag of mattress springs that she and Mateo had

64
00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:17.172
gotten. Next she found a package of magnets they'd used while redecorating the diner.

65
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:25.037
going to glue a magnet on one end of this spring," Ally said.

66
00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:29.800
"Then you'll slip your finger through the spring on the other end."

67
00:04:31.268 --> 00:04:33.570
"So the magnet will stick to the plate?"

68
00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:34.591
Barry asked.

69
00:04:34.611 --> 00:04:40.275
"How?" "Um Ally had forgotten that detail.

70
00:04:40.295 --> 00:04:44.878
"We put another magnet on the bottom of the plate, of course!

71
00:04:48.941 --> 00:04:52.363
Why don't you take care of the customers, and I'll get this trick set up."

72
00:04:55.185 --> 00:04:58.428
After Ally had gotten everything together, she called Barry back over.

73
00:05:00.976 --> 00:05:02.898
"Practice with a paper plate.

74
00:05:03.779 --> 00:05:07.762
That way you can get the feel of the trick, without breaking anything."

75
00:05:10.605 --> 00:05:14.128
Barry slipped the spring through his finger and then took a practice stumble.

76
00:05:16.009 --> 00:05:18.351
Ally was relieved when the plate stayed on the spring.

77
00:05:22.635 --> 00:05:24.617
He spun toward her, his eyes narrowed.

78
00:05:25.598 --> 00:05:27.900
"Why don't I ever see the spring when you do it?

79
00:05:28.788 --> 00:05:30.970
And how do you stick magnets to customers' plates?"

80
00:05:33.492 --> 00:05:35.293
Ally crossed her fingers behind her back.

81
00:05:35.994 --> 00:05:38.056
"I've been practicing a long time.

82
00:05:38.496 --> 00:05:39.897
You'll have to practice a lot.

83
00:05:40.598 --> 00:05:43.040
And remember, use paper plates for now!"

84
00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.602
She hurried off to take care of customers.

85
00:05:48.744 --> 00:05:53.068
A minute later she saw Barry stumble, a bowl of cold cereal attached to the spring.

86
00:05:53.748 --> 00:05:55.650
At first it looked like the trick was going to work.

87
00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.352
But then he lost his footing and tripped for real.

88
00:06:01.472 --> 00:06:03.837
The bowl flew through the air—and splash!

89
00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.263
It landed in a customer's lap!
